# 9. ALLIED SQUAD SYSTEM

The player should not fight alone.

Create AI-controlled allied mechs that accompany the player.

The player should be able to issue squad commands.

Commands should include:

- Follow me.
- Hold position.
- Attack my target.
- Defend this location.
- Spread out.
- Regroup.
- Retreat.
- Focus on a specific enemy.

Each squadmate should have:
- Its own health.
- Its own weapon.
- Its own movement physics.
- Its own personality or combat behavior.
- Its own targeting logic.
- Independent damage and ammunition status.

Squadmates should avoid stacking directly on top of one another.

Use formation positioning and separation behavior to make the squad move naturally.

They should maintain reasonable spacing, avoid obstacles, and attempt to support the player.

Allied AI should be useful rather than constantly getting stuck or requiring continuous player commands.

